1.	Dynamic Form Submission & Validation
Problem Statement: Write a Selenium script to navigate to a registration page, fill in text fields (Name, Email, Password), select a country from a standard <select> dropdown by visible text, check a "Terms & Conditions" checkbox only if it is not already selected, and click Submit.
Evaluation Criteria:
Proper use of Select class (selectByVisibleText()).
Conditional check using isSelected() before clicking the checkbox.
Verification of a success message after submission.

2.	Handling JavaScript Alerts & Pop-ups
Problem Statement: Automate a scenario where clicking a button triggers a JavaScript Confirmation Alert. Print the alert text to the console, accept the alert, and then trigger a Prompt Alert, enter "Automation Test" into it, and dismiss it.
Evaluation Criteria:
Switching context using driver.switchTo().alert().
Correct usage of getText(), accept(), sendKeys(), and dismiss().

3.	Multi-Window / Tab Handling
Problem Statement: Open a webpage containing a link that opens in a new browser tab. Click the link, switch to the newly opened tab, extract and print its page title, close the new tab, and switch control back to the parent window.
Evaluation Criteria:
Capturing parent window ID via getWindowHandle().
Iterating through getWindowHandles() to identify and switch to the child window.
Closing only the active tab (driver.close()) rather than the entire session (driver.quit()), followed by switching back to the parent handle.

